The Editor
*Energy and Buildings*

Dear Editor,

I am pleased to submit my manuscript, *Can a fine-tuned language model generate time-use diaries for a
country without survey data? A pre-registered test against reweighted real diaries*, for consideration
as an Original Paper in *Energy and Buildings*.

Occupancy schedules in building energy models are built from national time-use surveys, yet many
countries have no such survey or restrict access to it. A recent proposal is to fine-tune a language
model on the countries that have diaries and let it generate diaries for one that does not. I tested
this proposal against the alternative a modeller would actually use: real diaries from the other
countries, reweighted to the target country's published population margins. The study uses 73,254
diaries from the Harmonised European Time Use Survey for Spain, Italy and the UK. Each country is held
out in turn; the model is trained on the other two and conditioned only on the held-out country's
published margins.

The fine-tuned model does not beat reweighting real diaries. Its time-budget error is 1.1 to 3.9 times
that of the reweighted diaries in all nine country-by-age cells. It also misses the absolute accuracy
bar on the countries it was trained on, with a worst-age-band error of 33 to 158 % against a 15 % bar
that real diaries meet at 5 to 12 %, so the shortfall is not only a transfer effect. Carried into
activity-triggered appliance loads, the generated diaries do not carry each country's appliance timing:
real diaries place the evening electricity peak between 18:00 and 21:00, in a different country order
from the generated diaries.

For building energy modelling, occupancy sets internal gains, appliance and hot-water loads, and the
timing of peaks. The paper gives modellers a tested default for countries without diaries: reweighted
real diaries from comparable countries are the stronger starting point, and any generated diaries should
be checked against them before use.

The comparison, its metrics, tolerances and baseline were registered internally before training
(hash-locked, 2026-08-18) and are deposited at submission. The result is reported against that
unchanged bar.

The manuscript is original, has not been published previously, and is not under consideration
elsewhere. I have no competing interests to declare. The use of generative AI tools is declared at the
end of the manuscript.

